+# Carrier email — "Post your truck every morning" (drafted 5 Sep 2026)
+
+**Send AFTER** `bl_avail_0320` is on production and the carrier app is deployed (the email links to a
+button that only exists after deploy). Owner sends — from **hello@loadboot.com**, or via CC → Campaigns →
+audience "Active carriers". Companion HTML: `docs/CARRIER-EMAIL-DAILY-AVAILABILITY.html`.
+
+Suggested audience (prod, 5 Sep): real active carriers only — skip test/junk orgs (`Carrier Account`,
+`Loadboot`, `Rachel_0307`, single-word test names). Pilot names first: WARREN'S COURIER AGENCY, GABE
+LOGISTICS, MUNSTER, EZHAUL, JMS EXPRESS, PRIME FREIGHT, A&B GLOBAL, PATTERSON.
+
+---
+
+## Subject options (pick one)
+
+1. `Your dispatcher can only work a truck we can see — post it every morning`
+2. `New in your LoadBoot app: 30-second daily availability (and why it gets you more loads)`
+3. `<Company> — where is your truck this morning?`
+
+Preheader: `Empty or booked, one tap a day keeps your dedicated dispatcher on your loads.`
+
+---
+
+## Plain-text body
+
+Hi <First name>,
+
+A quick, important change in how we dispatch for <Company>.
+
+Your dedicated LoadBoot dispatcher can only sell a truck they can see. When we do not know
+where your truck is this morning — or where it delivers and when it frees up — we are
+guessing, and guessing loses loads to the carrier who told their dispatcher first.
+
+So starting today, your dispatcher works your loads ONLY while your truck's availability is
+posted and confirmed in the app within the last 24 hours. No fresh post, no sourcing. It is
+that simple, and it is the same rule the best fleets already run internally.
+
+WHAT TO DO — 30 SECONDS, EVERY MORNING
+
+1. Open the LoadBoot app → Load Board → "Post your availability"
+   https://loadboot.com/app/carrier/#loads
+2. Pick your situation:
+   • Truck is EMPTY — tell us the city it sits in and how far you will drive to pick up.
+   • Truck is BOOKED — tell us where it DELIVERS, the delivery date, and where you want the
+     backhaul to go (home base, or a state). We start working the reload before you unload.
+3. Tomorrow morning, tap "✓ Still available today" if nothing changed, or update it if the
+   truck moved. Posts expire every 24 hours on purpose — a stale post is worse than none.
+
+You will need at least one truck and one driver in your Fleet tab before you can post. If
+they are missing, the app takes you straight there.
+
+WHY THIS AND NOT WHATSAPP / EMAIL
+
+Because by the time a message is read, the load is gone. A posted truck is matched against
+every load on our board the second it goes live, alerts you automatically, and puts your
+truck in front of your dispatcher AND every shipper and broker posting into that lane.
+
+Your Dashboard now shows one of three states so there is never any doubt:
+  • Dispatcher working your loads (confirmed today)
+  • Confirm today (your post is over 24 hours old)
+  • Dispatcher paused (nothing posted)
+
+Post it this morning and your dispatcher starts on it today.
+
+Reply to this email or message us if anything is unclear.
+
+Muhammad Yaseen
+LoadBoot · loadboot.com · hello@loadboot.com
+
+---
+
+## WhatsApp / SMS short version
+
+LoadBoot update for <Company>: your dedicated dispatcher now works your loads only while your
+truck availability is posted in the app and confirmed within 24h. Empty → post the city.
+Booked → post where you deliver + where you want the backhaul. 30 seconds every morning:
+loadboot.com/app/carrier/#loads — post it today and we start sourcing today.
