Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Haul type: OTR/Regional/Local SEO pages, carrier
 haul_types preference, matcher band rule + Dispatch-tab persistence fix
 (bl_haul_0323, bl_fix_0324)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SEO: three new pages built from the existing svc_page pattern with their own frames, meta and facts
(otr-dispatch, regional-truck-dispatch, local-truck-dispatch) — the site had zero coverage of these
keywords; 'OTR' appeared once, as a factoring company name. Internal links, footer column, sitemap.

Portal: carriers were never asked how they run — it was inferred from home_time and trip miles.
carrier_dispatch_prefs.haul_types[] (local/regional/otr), asked in the Account Dispatch tab and in
onboarding with the bands printed on the chip; shown in Carrier 360. Empty = no filter.

Matcher: app_private.haul_band(miles) (local <=250, regional <=800, otr >800) + an additive rule in
tp_load_matches — only bites when the carrier stated a preference AND the load has miles.

BUG FIX (confirmed on production): cc_set_dispatch_prefs never persisted target_rpm, max_weight_lbs,
min_trip_miles, max_trip_miles, min_notice_hours or avoid_states — the Dispatch tab has been sending
them for months into a column list that did not include them. All 25 prod prefs rows have those
fields NULL. Now written, present-key-only so no caller can wipe what it does not send.

STAGING REPAIR (bl_fix_0324): public.loads.is_demo was missing on staging while tp_match_new_load
selects on it, so every load insert on staging failed with 42703. Column added to match production.

